{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"faa9261e-b9b6-4467-b98f-9d2e35801ad5","title":"Definite integral as the area under a curve"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"faa9261e-b9b6-4467-b98f-9d2e35801ad5","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A definite integral measures signed area between a curve and the horizontal axis. Start with this curve, which stays above zero.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Definite integral = signed area"},{"op":"figure","id":"plot","region":"right","frame":{"x":[0,3.3],"y":[0,10],"axes":"edge","x_label":"x","y_label":"f(x)"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"curve","y":"x^2","domain":[0,3],"label":"f(x) = x²"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"target","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\int_1^3 x^2\\,dx"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"faa9261e-b9b6-4467-b98f-9d2e35801ad5","step":{"id":"s2","script":"The limits one and three mark the interval. Shade only the region between those boundaries, the curve, and the axis.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"region","on":"plot","marks":[{"kind":"shade","id":"area","under":"curve","from":1,"to":3,"label":"A"},{"kind":"point","id":"lower","at":{"on":"curve","x":1}},{"kind":"point","id":"upper","at":{"on":"curve","x":3}},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"lower"},"to":[1,0],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"upper"},"to":[3,0],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"text","at":[1,0.35],"text":"1"},{"kind":"text","at":[3,0.35],"text":"3"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"areaeq","anchor":{"el":"target","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"A=\\int_1^3 x^2\\,dx"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"faa9261e-b9b6-4467-b98f-9d2e35801ad5","step":{"id":"s3","script":"An antiderivative gives the exact area: evaluate at the upper limit, then subtract its value at the lower limit.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"evaluate","anchor":{"el":"areaeq","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"A=\\left[\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right]_1^3=9-\\frac13=\\frac{26}{3}"},{"op":"figure","id":"resultmark","on":"plot","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[2.35,2.1],"text":"26/3","size":"large"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"faa9261e-b9b6-4467-b98f-9d2e35801ad5","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Here the integral equals ordinary area because the curve is positive. Below the axis, contributions would be negative.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"conclusion","anchor":{"el":"evaluate","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"Above axis: positive. Below: negative."},{"op":"figure","id":"positive","on":"plot","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[2.35,3.2],"text":"+","size":"large"}]}],"checkpoint":{"question":"If the same region were reflected below the horizontal axis, what would its definite integral be?","expected_gist":"Negative 26/3; the geometric area remains 26/3, but the integral is signed."}}}
